    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, as the code currently stands. The endpoint is implemented as an OfficeFloor pipeline (`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 there are no `@RestController`/`@ControllerAdvice` classes. The OfficeFloor Boot-4 starter *is* in `pom.xml`, so the pipeline is live.\n\n## 0. Gate (before the pipeline)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role \u2192 403 (`AuthorizationDeniedException` handler).\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n**1. `route` \u2014 RouteIdempotentCreate**\n- Side-effect / branch: reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was seen before *and* the owner still exists, it republishes the existing `Owner` and branches to `respondExisting` \u2192 **RespondWithOwner (200)**, short-circuiting everything below. Otherwise it publishes the key (`\"\"` if absent) and continues.\n\n**2. `require` \u2014 RequireOwnerFields**\n- Validation: binds the `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the **only** body-binding step, and it does **not** use `@Valid`). Manually checks presence of firstName, lastName, address (structured `addressLine1` or flat `address`), city, telephone. Missing any \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400** (`{\"errors\":[...]}`). Republishes the DTO.\n\n**3. `normalize` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerTelephone**\n- Side-effect: rewrites `telephone` to E.164 (`+<digits>`; assumes `+61` if no `+`, drops a leading 0).\n- Validation: enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length (+61\u21929, +1\u219210). Otherwise \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException([\"telephone\"])` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**4. `normalizeEmail` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerEmail**\n- Side-effect: if email present, lower-cases it.\n- Validation: must match a basic email regex, else \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException([\"email\"])` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**5. `rejectDisposableEmail` \u2014 RejectDisposableEmailDomain**\n- Validation: blocks `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**6. `normalizeAddress` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerAddress**\n- Side-effect: canonicalizes address (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expands ST/RD/AVE); prefers structured address lines. No rejection.\n\n**7. `rejectDuplicate` \u2014 RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity**\n- Validation: scans `ownerRepository.findAll()` (skipping soft-deleted) for a matching `IdentityKey.of(telephone, email)` \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n**8. `rejectCrowdedCity` \u2014 RejectCrowdedCity**\n- Validation: \u226550 existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CrowdedCityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n**9. `rejectDailyLimit` \u2014 RejectDailyLimit**\n- Validation: \u2265100 owners with today's (business-day) registrationDate \u2192 `DailyLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n**10. `rejectInvalidPostcode` \u2014 RejectInvalidPostcode**\n- Validation: 4-digit postcode plus region-range check (NSW/VIC/QLD via `Locality`) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**11. `rejectFutureDate` \u2014 RejectFutureRegistrationDate**\n- Validation: registrationDate after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n--- from here on every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]` (one commit at the end) ---\n\n**12. `build` \u2014 BuildOwner**\n- Validation: class is `@Validated` and the method takes `@Valid @Val OwnerFieldsDto`, so the DTO's bean-validation constraints run **here** (firstName/lastName `@Pattern`+`@Size`, city, postcode `^[0-9]{4}$`, telephone `^[0-9]*$` + `@Size(max=20)`, etc.). Failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400** ProblemDetail with `schemaValidationErrors`.\n- Side-effect: maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` (via `OwnerMapper`), defaults registrationDate and rolls it to a business day; publishes `Out<Owner>`.\n\n**13. `assignCustomerCode` \u2014 AssignCustomerCode**\n- Side-effect: sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>` (SHA-256 of telephone + lastName).\n\n**14. `deduplicateCustomerCode` \u2014 DeduplicateCustomerCode**\n- Side-effect: appends `-n` on customerCode collision.\n\n**15. `countNamesakes` \u2014 CountNamesakes**\n- Side-effect: sets `namesakeCount` (existing owners with same first+last, case-insensitive).\n\n**16. `detectPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 DetectPossibleDuplicate**\n- Side-effect: flags a soft duplicate by `HouseholdId` (lastName+postcode) with a different telephone, unless `sharesHousehold` is true; sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`. (No rejection \u2014 a flag only.)\n\n**17. `save` \u2014 SaveOwner**\n- Side-effect: `ownerRepository.save(owner)` plus an AUDIT log (computes membership number/level).\n\n**18. `record` \u2014 RecordIdempotencyKey**\n- Side-effect: stores `key \u2192 ownerId` in the `IdempotencyStore` (backs step 1 on retries).\n\n**19. `respond` \u2014 RespondWithOwnerCreated**\n- Side-effect: maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning`, responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Two things worth flagging (not changed)\n\n1. **Telephone validation is contradictory.** Step 3 rewrites telephone into E.164 (`+61\u2026`), but the DTO constraint checked at step 12 (`BuildOwner`, `@Valid`) is `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]*$\")` \u2014 digits only, no `+`. If `@Valid` fires on the `@Val` parameter, an otherwise-valid request is rejected at step 12 with a 400. (The `Owner` *entity* separately requires E.164 `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, the opposite constraint.) So the DTO and entity telephone rules disagree, and the normalization sits between them.\n\n2. **The DTO's own bean-validation is deferred.** Because step 2 binds the body without `@Valid`, all the `@Pattern`/`@Size`/`@NotNull` DTO constraints do not run until step 12 \u2014 after telephone/email/address have already been mutated by steps 3\u20136. The early rejections (steps 2\u201311) are all hand-written checks, not the annotation constraints.\n\nNothing was modified."
